From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 18:08:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07853/11362] [outer-loop] CORRIGENDUM exp5835: conclusion VOID
 -- unpassable gate + clock label; object perception was never actually tested

Three independently re-verified defects void the experiment (original numbers preserved):
D1 the pre-registered gate required order1_auc<=0.56 (an ASSUMPTION about the baseline)
   as a conjunct, so with measured order1=0.6898 gate_clears was False for ANY object
   value including a perfect 1.00 -- zero information about object perception.
D2 level_progress(row, step_index) never reads the frame; the measured task is trajectory
   POSITION, not perception.
D3 a step_index-ONLY predictor scores 0.9234 LOO-AUC on the same label, beating both
   feature arms (0.6898 / 0.6564) -- both 'perception' arms lose to a clock.

RETRACTED: that object-level perception was tested or ruled out; and that order-1 is
'a decent 0.69 for progress prediction' (largely clock leakage; the GAP-4891
order-1-at-chance finding is NOT narrowed by this experiment).

Lesson: never encode an assumption about the BASELINE as a pass-requirement for the
TREATMENT; and verify the label actually depends on the featurized input (the trivial
step-index positive control would have caught this pre-run).

